1
00:00:00,220 --> 00:00:01,280
Speaker 0: Morning everyone!

2
00:00:02,440 --> 00:00:05,340
Speaker 0: Let's review our action items from the last meeting.

3
00:00:06,440 --> 00:00:08,940
Speaker 0: Ramesh, start with the syllabus submission.

4
00:00:10,620 --> 00:00:13,300
Speaker 2: Submitted to the Board of Studies on time.

5
00:00:14,300 --> 00:00:15,780
Speaker 2: They reviewed it yesterday.

6
00:00:16,780 --> 00:00:18,340
Speaker 2: Generally positive feedback.

7
00:00:19,460 --> 00:00:20,480
Speaker 2: One concern though.

8
00:00:21,480 --> 00:00:27,440
Speaker 2: They want the assessment to include a hands-on project component, not just a written exam.

9
00:00:29,180 --> 00:00:30,240
Speaker 0: That's a fair point.

10
00:00:31,400 --> 00:00:32,299
Speaker 0: What are you thinking?

11
00:00:33,960 --> 00:00:36,820
Speaker 2: A mini project worth 30%.

12
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:40,400
Speaker 2: Students deploy a deep learning model to production.

13
00:00:41,400 --> 00:00:44,640
Speaker 2: Maybe on AWS free tier or Google Cloud.

14
00:00:45,620 --> 00:00:48,800
Speaker 2: It tests practical skills better than an exam.

15
00:00:50,420 --> 00:00:51,480
Speaker 3: That's a good idea.

16
00:00:52,620 --> 00:00:56,200
Speaker 3: My students keep complaining that exams don't reflect real work.

17
00:00:57,920 --> 00:00:58,400
Speaker 0: Approved.

18
00:00:59,540 --> 00:01:02,240
Speaker 0: Revise the assessment breakdown and resubmit.

19
00:01:03,400 --> 00:01:05,019
Speaker 0: When's the next BOS meeting?

20
00:01:06,620 --> 00:01:07,660
Speaker 2: Two weeks from now.

21
00:01:08,740 --> 00:01:10,020
Speaker 2: I'll have the revision ready.

22
00:01:11,780 --> 00:01:12,000
Speaker 0: Good.

23
00:01:13,100 --> 00:01:14,600
Speaker 0: Avan, the lab upgrade.

24
00:01:16,220 --> 00:01:17,480
Speaker 1: Ma'am, there's a problem.

25
00:01:18,500 --> 00:01:21,880
Speaker 1: The GPU prices have gone up significantly in the last two weeks.

26
00:01:22,920 --> 00:01:25,540
Speaker 1: The Dell quote I had was valid for seven days only.

27
00:01:26,680 --> 00:01:30,060
Speaker 1: New quotes are coming in at about 1.12 Lakhs per machine.

28
00:01:31,760 --> 00:01:33,920
Speaker 0: That's a 35% increase.

29
00:01:34,940 --> 00:01:35,680
Speaker 0: Total cost?

30
00:01:37,320 --> 00:01:40,020
Speaker 1: For four machines, it comes to 4.5 lakhs.

31
00:01:41,120 --> 00:01:43,500
Speaker 1: About one and a half lakh over our approved budget.

32
00:01:45,120 --> 00:01:47,800
Speaker 2: Can we delay the elective launch by a semester?

33
00:01:49,540 --> 00:01:52,320
Speaker 0: No, we've already advertised it to students.

34
00:01:53,380 --> 00:01:55,280
Speaker 0: Bhavan, what are our options?

35
00:01:57,040 --> 00:01:57,660
Speaker 1: I see two.

36
00:01:58,860 --> 00:02:00,220
Speaker 1: One, reduce the quantity.

37
00:02:01,300 --> 00:02:04,160
Speaker 1: Buy two now at 2.2 lakhs, two more next quarter.

38
00:02:05,240 --> 00:02:08,500
Speaker 1: Two, look at refurbished or academic edition workstations.

39
00:02:09,600 --> 00:02:12,560
Speaker 1: Some vendors offer academic pricing at 20% off.

40
00:02:14,400 --> 00:02:16,280
Speaker 0: I prefer option 1.

41
00:02:16,760 --> 00:02:17,920
Speaker 0: Splitting the purchase.

42
00:02:19,020 --> 00:02:21,580
Speaker 0: Students can share machines in the first run.

43
00:02:22,780 --> 00:02:24,720
Speaker 0: Submit the revised proposal today.

44
00:02:25,840 --> 00:02:29,140
Speaker 0: Approved for 2.2 lakhs for phase 1 procurement.

45
00:02:30,900 --> 00:02:31,260
Speaker 1: Will do.

46
00:02:32,560 --> 00:02:35,080
Speaker 1: I'll also ask about academic pricing for phase 2.

47
00:02:36,920 --> 00:02:37,540
Speaker 0: Good thinking.

48
00:02:38,720 --> 00:02:41,360
Speaker 0: Now, Meera, the capstone extension.

49
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:45,120
Speaker 3: The extension has helped most teams.

50
00:02:46,180 --> 00:02:48,860
Speaker 3: But five teams still haven't submitted phase one.

51
00:02:49,900 --> 00:02:52,240
Speaker 3: The new deadline is December 22nd.

52
00:02:53,320 --> 00:02:56,800
Speaker 3: Three of them told me they are still finalizing the problem statement.

53
00:02:58,560 --> 00:02:59,760
Speaker 0: That's not acceptable.

54
00:03:00,840 --> 00:03:03,460
Speaker 0: The extension was two weeks, not unlimited.

55
00:03:04,520 --> 00:03:05,620
Speaker 0: Who are these teams?

56
00:03:07,240 --> 00:03:11,340
Speaker 3: Team 7, 12, 15, 18, and 23.

57
00:03:12,820 --> 00:03:14,540
Speaker 0: Send them a warning email today.

58
00:03:15,640 --> 00:03:21,260
Speaker 0: If they don't submit by December 22nd, they fail Phase 1 and redo it next semester.

59
00:03:22,400 --> 00:03:23,620
Speaker 0: No more extensions.

60
00:03:25,240 --> 00:03:25,680
Speaker 3: Agreed.

61
00:03:26,760 --> 00:03:28,460
Speaker 3: I'll send the notice this afternoon.

62
00:03:30,160 --> 00:03:32,760
Speaker 2: What about teams that have submitted already?

63
00:03:33,800 --> 00:03:35,140
Speaker 2: Are they getting feedback?

64
00:03:36,820 --> 00:03:37,080
Speaker 3: Yes.

65
00:03:38,200 --> 00:03:40,100
Speaker 3: I'm reviewing 8 submissions this week.

66
00:03:41,240 --> 00:03:42,960
Speaker 3: Feedback goes out by Friday.

67
00:03:44,700 --> 00:03:46,900
Speaker 0: Bhavan, the TCS Drive update.

68
00:03:48,480 --> 00:03:49,980
Speaker 1: The TCS drive is done.

69
00:03:51,020 --> 00:03:52,460
Speaker 1: Happened on the 8th as planned.

70
00:03:52,480 --> 00:03:55,020
Speaker 1: 42 students appeared.

71
00:03:55,040 --> 00:03:57,840
Speaker 1: 18 cleared the technical round.

72
00:03:58,980 --> 00:04:00,880
Speaker 1: Final results announced last Monday.

73
00:04:00,900 --> 00:04:03,240
Speaker 1: 12 offers extended.

74
00:04:03,260 --> 00:04:07,060
Speaker 2: 12 offers out of 42.

75
00:04:07,840 --> 00:04:10,180
Speaker 2: That's a 28% conversion.

76
00:04:11,220 --> 00:04:13,940
Speaker 2: Better than last year's 20%.

77
00:04:15,140 --> 00:04:15,660
Speaker 1: Correct.

78
00:04:16,720 --> 00:04:18,360
Speaker 1: The mock interview sessions helped.

79
00:04:19,480 --> 00:04:26,720
Speaker 1: Students who attended both sessions had a 60% pass rate in the technical round, compared to 35% for those who didn't attend.

80
00:04:28,400 --> 00:04:33,740
Speaker 3: We should make the mock sessions mandatory for all students then, not just TCS candidates.

81
00:04:35,480 --> 00:04:36,200
Speaker 0: Good proposal.

82
00:04:37,340 --> 00:04:39,580
Speaker 0: Let me discuss with the placement committee.

83
00:04:40,700 --> 00:04:42,740
Speaker 0: What's next on the recruitment calendar?

84
00:04:44,440 --> 00:04:46,900
Speaker 1: Enthosis is confirmed for January 15th.

85
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:49,700
Speaker 1: Wipro for January 20th.

86
00:04:50,800 --> 00:04:52,180
Speaker 1: Accenture is still pending.

87
00:04:53,220 --> 00:04:54,820
Speaker 1: They promised a date by next week.

88
00:04:56,560 --> 00:04:58,780
Speaker 0: Follow up with Accenture by Wednesday.

89
00:04:59,920 --> 00:05:02,900
Speaker 0: If they don't confirm, we schedule someone else.

90
00:05:03,920 --> 00:05:05,540
Speaker 0: Can't keep that slot open.

91
00:05:07,320 --> 00:05:08,280
Speaker 1: I'll call them tomorrow.

92
00:05:10,160 --> 00:05:10,980
Speaker 0: One more item.

93
00:05:12,100 --> 00:05:15,460
Speaker 0: The department website hasn't been updated since last year.

94
00:05:16,580 --> 00:05:18,480
Speaker 0: Faculty profiles are outdated.

95
00:05:19,520 --> 00:05:21,360
Speaker 0: Course pages show old syllabi.

96
00:05:22,600 --> 00:05:24,800
Speaker 0: This looks bad during admission season.

97
00:05:26,580 --> 00:05:30,460
Speaker 2: I can assign two of my student assistants to update the content.

98
00:05:31,460 --> 00:05:32,940
Speaker 2: They're good at web stuff.

99
00:05:33,980 --> 00:05:35,340
Speaker 2: Should take three weeks.

100
00:05:36,980 --> 00:05:37,420
Speaker 0: Please do.

101
00:05:38,620 --> 00:05:42,180
Speaker 0: We need it ready before February when admission queries pick up.

102
00:05:43,280 --> 00:05:47,740
Speaker 0: Meera, can you coordinate with them on the NLP and AI course pages?

103
00:05:49,420 --> 00:05:49,660
Speaker 3: Yes.

104
00:05:50,760 --> 00:05:53,640
Speaker 3: I'll give them the updated content by end of this week.

105
00:05:55,420 --> 00:05:55,760
Speaker 0: Great!

106
00:05:56,880 --> 00:05:57,640
Speaker 0: Anything else?

107
00:05:58,760 --> 00:05:58,840
Speaker 0: No?

108
00:06:00,100 --> 00:06:00,820
Speaker 0: Let's wrap up.

109
00:06:01,960 --> 00:06:03,680
Speaker 0: Next meeting, February 2nd.

110
00:06:04,780 --> 00:06:07,280
Speaker 0: Thank you, everyone.

